\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father, who art alone
\par Our helper and our stay,
\par O hear us, as we plead
\par For loved ones far away,
\par And shield with Thine almighty hand
\par Our wanderers by sea and land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For Thou, our Father God,
\par Art present everywhere,
\par And bendest low Thine ear
\par To catch the faintest prayer,
\par Waiting rich blessings to bestow
\par On all Thy children here below.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O compass with Thy love
\par The daily path they tread;
\par And may Thy light and truth
\par Upon their hearts be shed,
\par That, one all things with Thy will,
\par Heaven's peace and joy their souls may fill.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Guard them from every harm
\par When dangers shall assail,
\par And teach them that Thy power
\par Can never, never fail;
\par We cannot with our loved ones be,
\par But trust them, Father, unto Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. We all are travellers here
\par Along life's various raod,
\par Meeting and parting oft
\par Till we shall mount to God,
\par At home at last, with those we love,
\par Within the fatherland above.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

